"The Software" is the BootyBayBroker Ferryman addon for World of Warcraft: the
folders BootyBayBrokerFerryman, BootyBayBrokerFerryman_EasternKingdoms and
BootyBayBrokerFerryman_Kalimdor and everything in them (code, artwork and data
files), together with the other files of this repository. Its source is
published so that anyone can read it.

1. What you may do

Free of charge, and for as long as you keep to these terms, you may:

  - download the Software from a place where the copyright holder publishes it
    (this repository, its releases, or an addon site the copyright holder has
    listed it on), directly or through an addon manager that fetches it from
    such a place;
  - install it and run it in World of Warcraft, for your own play, and keep
    copies for that;
  - read its source.

2. What you may not do

Every other right is reserved. Without the copyright holder's prior written
permission you may not:

  - redistribute the Software or any part of it, changed or unchanged, on any
    addon site, repository, service or medium;
  - publish, upload or offer a changed version, a renamed copy or a derivative
    work;
  - use its code, its artwork or its data files in another addon, program or
    dataset;
  - sell it, charge for access to it, or bundle it with anything that is sold.

3. GitHub

GitHub's Terms of Service let GitHub host this repository and let its users
view it and fork it on GitHub. These terms do not restrict that. A fork gives
no right beyond section 1, with one exception: you may change your fork on
GitHub only to offer that change to the copyright holder in a pull request to
this repository, and the change is then a contribution under section 5. A fork
is not permission to publish changes or to distribute copies anywhere else, and
it must keep this file and the copyright notice as they are.

4. Other addons

Another addon may call the functions the Software offers to other addons (its
global "Ferryman") where a player has installed both. That is use of the
Software, not a copy of it. It does not permit putting the Software, or any
part of it, in another addon's package or download: a player gets the Software
only from a place named in section 1, as an addon manager does when it installs
it as another addon's dependency.

5. Contributions

If you send the copyright holder a change, a translation, a correction or a
suggestion for the Software (for example as a pull request or an issue), you
give the copyright holder a perpetual, irrevocable, worldwide, royalty-free
licence to use, copy, change, distribute and sublicense it, in the Software or
in any other work, under any terms, with no obligation to you. You confirm that
it is yours to give.

6. Ending

Your rights under section 1 end at once if you break these terms. You must then
stop using the Software and delete your copies of it.

